# Smoke test for the ELPA width-1 tail block bug family (cp2k issue #4484).
#
# With an unfixed ELPA (<= 2026.02.002 without the bugfix_elpa2_65_65_64 patch),
# this input deadlocks in the first OT FULL_ALL preconditioner:
#   1. the MO subspace diagonalization has na = nocc = 129 = 2*nbw+1 (258 valence
#      electrons, nbw=64), so tridiag_band's width-1 tail block emits an orphan
#      one-vector Isend (tag 10+2) that no MPI_irecv ever matches,
#   2. the following T-matrix diagonalization (na = nao = 746) posts an irecv with
#      the same tag, which consumes the orphan; its real 94 KB chunk is then left
#      unmatched and the two ranks deadlock (ELPA issue #83, cross-call tag reuse).
#
# Requirements met by construction: nocc == 1 (mod nbw), nocc >= 2*nbw+1,
# nao >= 5*nbw. Triggers at 2 MPI ranks (the do_regtest default); the deadlock
# happens before the first OT step, so convergence settings are irrelevant.
# No matcher: on a fixed ELPA the run simply completes (a few seconds); on a
# broken one it hangs and gets killed by the test timeout.
&GLOBAL
  PRINT_LEVEL LOW
  PROJECT tailblock_hang
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
&END GLOBAL

&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    BASIS_SET_FILE_NAME BASIS_MOLOPT
    POTENTIAL_FILE_NAME POTENTIAL
    &SCF
      # Smoke test: the deadlock (if any) happens before the first OT step.
      IGNORE_CONVERGENCE_FAILURE
      MAX_SCF 3
      &OT
        MINIMIZER DIIS
        PRECONDITIONER FULL_ALL
      &END OT
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PBE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      A 15.0 0.0 0.0
      B 0.0 15.0 0.0
      C 0.0 0.0 15.0
      PERIODIC NONE
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      H 2.845110 0.701321 5.609701
      H 2.492648 0.625335 3.851516
      O 2.390131 0.853920 4.778252
      H 2.404075 1.126963 10.817552
      H 2.986300 1.081558 10.674129
